   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# XGBoost Machine Learning Pipeline: Disease Burden & Mortality Risk Prediction\n",
    "## Clinical-Epidemiological Framework using XGBoost Regressor & Classifier\n",
    "\n",
    "### Project Overview\n",
    "This notebook implements a **two-path machine learning pipeline** to predict health outcomes using socio-environmental and demographic features:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Path A (Regression)**: Predict `total_diagnoses` (disease burden count) using XGBRegressor\n",
    "- **Path B (Classification)**: Predict `is_deceased` (mortality risk) using XGBClassifier with imbalance handling\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Challenges Addressed\n",
    "1. **Zero-inflated count data** (Path A ceiling effect)\n",
    "2. **Extreme class imbalance** (1.9% minority class in Path B)\n",
    "3. **Information bottleneck** (demographics vs. clinical features)\n",
    "4. **Model generalization** (overfitting in small datasets)\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 0: Data Loading & Initial Exploration\n",
    "\n",
    "Load the dataset and perform basic exploratory data analysis to understand the structure and distributions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import xgboost as xgb\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
    "    mean_squared_error, r2_score, \n",
    "    roc_auc_score, average_precision_score, \n",
    "    confusion_matrix, classification_report, \n",
    "    precision_recall_curve, precision_score, recall_score\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set visualization style\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\n",
    "plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (14, 6)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ All libraries imported successfully\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load the dataset from GitHub repository\n",
    "url = \"https://github.com/abhisakh/XGBOOST_Machine_Leraning_Predictor_Titanic/raw/main/NODE_A_unified.csv\"\ndf = pd.read_csv(url)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Display basic information\n",
    "print(f\"Dataset Shape: {df.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📊 First 5 Rows:\")\n",
    "print(df.head())\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📋 Data Types & Missing Values:\")\n",
    "print(df.info())\n",
    "print(f\"\\n🔍 Missing Values Summary:\")\n",
    "print(df.isnull().sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Part 1: Data Preparation & Feature Selection\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Principle: Avoid Data Leakage\n",
    "We separate our features into **input matrix (X)** and **target vectors (y)** while carefully excluding:\n",
    "- **Metadata** (patient IDs, timestamps)\n",
    "- **Zero-variance columns** (constant values, no predictive value)\n",
    "- **Downstream clinical leakage** (prescriptions, hospital stays) when predicting baseline disease burden\n",
    "\n",
    "### Feature Selection Strategy\n",
    "We use **15 baseline features** across four domains:\n",
    "1. **Demographics**: age, sex, region, urban_rural, education\n",
    "2. **Socioeconomic**: employment_status, income_quartile, estimated_income, migration_background\n",
    "3. **Insurance**: insurance_fund, insurance_status\n",
    "4. **Exposome (Environmental)**: air_quality, green_space, noise_level, deprivation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define the 15-feature baseline input matrix\n",
    "baseline_features = [\n",
    "    # Demographics (5 features)\n",
    "    'age', 'sex', 'region', 'urban_rural', 'education',\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Socioeconomic Context (4 features)\n",
    "    'employment_status', 'income_quartile', 'estimated_income', 'migration_background',\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Insurance Profile (2 features)\n",
    "    'insurance_fund', 'insurance_status',\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Exposome / Environmental Factors (4 features)\n",
    "    'exposome_air_quality', 'exposome_green_space', 'exposome_noise_level', 'exposome_deprivation'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Extract input matrix and target vectors\n",
    "X_baseline = df[baseline_features].copy()\n",
    "y_path_A = df['total_diagnoses'].copy()  # Target for Path A (Regression)\n",
    "y_path_B = df['is_deceased'].copy()      # Target for Path B (Classification)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✓ Input Matrix Shape: {X_baseline.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"✓ Path A Target Shape: {y_path_A.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"✓ Path B Target Shape: {y_path_B.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📊 Target Distributions:\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Path A (total_diagnoses) - Mean: {y_path_A.mean():.2f}, Std: {y_path_A.std():.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Path B (is_deceased) - Class Distribution:\\n{y_path_B.value_counts(normalize=True)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 1.1: Prepare Categorical Features for XGBoost\n",
    "\n",
    "XGBoost can handle **categorical variables natively** if they are explicitly cast to pandas `category` dtype.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why This Matters**: \n",
    "- Without proper categorical encoding, text columns are treated as numbers, breaking the model\n",
    "- Native categorical support prevents unnecessary one-hot encoding, preserving tree-based feature interactions\n",
    "- Must be done BEFORE train-test split to ensure consistent encoding across all splits"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Identify categorical (text/object) columns\n",
    "categorical_cols = X_baseline.select_dtypes(include=['object', 'category']).columns.tolist()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"🔍 Categorical Columns Found: {categorical_cols}\")\nprint(f\"\\n🔄 Converting to pandas 'category' dtype...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Convert text columns to category type for native XGBoost support\n",
    "for col in categorical_cols:\n",
    "    X_baseline[col] = X_baseline[col].astype('category')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✓ All categorical columns successfully converted\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📋 Updated Data Types:\")\n",
    "print(X_baseline.dtypes)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 1.2: Feature Engineering - Creating Interaction Terms\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why Feature Engineering?**\n",
    "\n",
    "XGBoost excels at finding non-linear relationships, but explicitly creating interaction features helps it:\n",
    "1. **Faster learning** - Doesn't waste trees discovering obvious interactions\n",
    "2. **Better interpretability** - Interaction terms map to real clinical mechanisms\n",
    "3. **Handle isolated subgroups** - Deeper splits for rare, high-risk populations\n",
    "\n",
    "**Our 5 Engineered Features:**\n",
    "| Feature | Formula | Clinical Meaning |\n",
    "|---------|---------|------------------|\n",
    "| `age_squared` | age² | Non-linear health degradation with aging |\n",
    "| `age_x_pollution` | age × air_quality | Vulnerable elderly in polluted zones |\n",
    "| `pollution_x_deprivation` | air_quality × deprivation | Poverty + pollution compound stress |\n",
    "| `urban_noise_stress` | noise_level × (1.5 if urban else 1.0) | Amplified urban acoustic strain |\n",
    "| `age_income_interaction` | age × income | Diverging health trajectories by wealth |\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create engineered feature matrix (will have 15 + 5 = 20 total features)\n",
    "X_engineered = X_baseline.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"🔧 Creating 5 Interaction Features...\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Feature 1: Non-linear age effect\n",
    "X_engineered['age_squared'] = X_engineered['age'] ** 2\n",
    "print(f\"1. age_squared: Captures accelerated health decline with aging\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Feature 2: Age-pollution vulnerability interaction\n",
    "X_engineered['age_x_pollution'] = X_engineered['age'] * X_engineered['exposome_air_quality']\n",
    "print(f\"2. age_x_pollution: Elderly patients exposed to poor air quality\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Feature 3: Environmental deprivation compound effect\n",
    "X_engineered['pollution_x_deprivation'] = X_engineered['exposome_air_quality'] * X_engineered['exposome_deprivation']\n",
    "print(f\"3. pollution_x_deprivation: High pollution + high poverty overlap\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Feature 4: Urban noise amplification\n",
    "urban_factor = np.where(X_engineered['urban_rural'] == 'urban', 1.5, 1.0)\n",
    "X_engineered['urban_noise_stress'] = X_engineered['exposome_noise_level'] * urban_factor\n",
    "print(f\"4. urban_noise_stress: Amplified noise effect in urban areas\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Feature 5: Age-income interaction (with safe type checking)\n",
    "if pd.api.types.is_numeric_dtype(X_engineered['estimated_income']):\n",
    "    X_engineered['age_income_interaction'] = X_engineered['age'] * X_engineered['estimated_income']\n",
    "    print(f\"5. age_income_interaction: Diverging health trajectories by income level\")\nelse:\n",
    "    # Fallback if income is categorical\n",
    "    X_engineered['age_income_interaction'] = X_engineered['age'] * X_engineered['exposome_deprivation']\n",
    "    print(f\"5. age_income_interaction (fallback): Age × deprivation proxy\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\n✓ Final Feature Matrix: {X_engineered.shape[1]} total features (15 baseline + 5 engineered)\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📊 Feature Engineering Summary:\")\n",
    "print(X_engineered[['age', 'age_squared', 'age_x_pollution', 'pollution_x_deprivation']].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Part 2: PATH A - Disease Burden Prediction (XGBoost Regressor)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Problem Statement\n",
    "**Predict**: `total_diagnoses` (count of active health conditions) for each patient\n",
    "\n",
    "**Challenge**: Count data with zero-inflation (many patients have 0-2 diagnoses)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Solution Strategy\n",
    "1. **Change loss function** from MSE to Tweedie (handles count data naturally)\n",
    "2. **Regularize aggressively** to prevent overfitting\n",
    "3. **Engineer features** to expose hidden patterns"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 2.1: Train-Test Split for Path A"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Split data: 80% training, 20% testing\n",
    "X_train_A, X_test_A, y_train_A, y_test_A = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X_engineered, y_path_A, test_size=0.2, random_state=42\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Re-enforce categorical dtypes after split\n",
    "cat_cols = X_train_A.select_dtypes(include=['object', 'category']).columns.tolist()\n",
    "for col in cat_cols:\n",
    "    X_train_A[col] = X_train_A[col].astype('category')\n",
    "    X_test_A[col] = X_test_A[col].astype('category')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✓ Path A Data Split Complete\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Training set:   {X_train_A.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Testing set:    {X_test_A.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Training target - Mean: {y_train_A.mean():.2f}, Std: {y_train_A.std():.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Testing target  - Mean: {y_test_A.mean():.2f}, Std: {y_test_A.std():.2f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 2.2: Train Optimized Tweedie Regressor\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why Tweedie?**\n",
    "- **Standard MSE Loss** assumes errors are normally distributed → causes \"ceiling effect\" at predictions ~30\n",
    "- **Tweedie Regression** bridges Poisson (for counts) and Gamma (for right-skewed tails)\n",
    "- **tweedie_variance_power=1.5** optimally balances zero-inflation with heavy right tail\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hyperparameter Rationale:**\n",
    "| Parameter | Value | Why? |\n",
    "|-----------|-------|------|\n",
    "| n_estimators | 250 | More trees to compensate for low learning rate |\n",
    "| learning_rate | 0.02 | Slow, conservative updates to prevent overfitting |\n",
    "| max_depth | 5 | Shallow trees to block memorization of noise |\n",
    "| subsample | 0.8 | Each tree sees random 80% of rows |\n",
    "| colsample_bytree | 0.8 | Each tree sees random 80% of features |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initialize optimized Tweedie regressor\n",
    "print(\"🚀 Training Optimized Tweedie Regressor...\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "model_A_tweedie = xgb.XGBRegressor(\n",
    "    n_estimators=250,              # Increased trees for slower learning\n",
    "    learning_rate=0.02,            # Very conservative step size\n",
    "    max_depth=5,                   # Shallow trees prevent overfitting\n",
    "    subsample=0.8,                 # 80% of rows per tree\n",
    "    colsample_bytree=0.8,          # 80% of features per tree\n",
    "    objective=\"reg:tweedie\",       # Count-friendly loss function\n",
    "    tweedie_variance_power=1.5,    # Balance Poisson-Gamma distributions\n",
    "    enable_categorical=True,       # Native categorical support\n",
    "    random_state=42,\n",
    "    verbosity=0\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Train the model\n",
    "model_A_tweedie.fit(X_train_A, y_train_A, verbose=False)\nprint(\"✓ Model training complete\")\n\n",
    "# Make predictions\n",
    "y_pred_A = model_A_tweedie.predict(X_test_A)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate performance metrics\n",
    "r2_A = r2_score(y_test_A, y_pred_A)\n",
    "rmse_A = np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(y_test_A, y_pred_A))\n",
    "residuals_A = y_test_A - y_pred_A\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📊 PATH A RESULTS (Tweedie Regressor):\")\n",
    "print(f\"═\" * 50)\n",
    "print(f\"R² Score (Coefficient of Determination): {r2_A:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"RMSE (Root Mean Squared Error):          {rmse_A:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📈 Residual Analysis:\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Mean Residual:  {residuals_A.mean():.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Std Residual:   {residuals_A.std():.4f}\")\nprint(f\"   Under-prediction: {np.mean(residuals_A > 0)*100:.1f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 2.3: Visualize Path A Results\n",
    "\n",
    "**Interpretation Guide:**\n",
    "- **Left plot**: Points close to diagonal = good predictions; scatter below diagonal = model is conservative\n",
    "- **Right plot**: Distribution centered at 0 = balanced errors; right-skewed = model under-predicts high values"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create comprehensive visualization\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(16, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 1: Prediction vs Actual\n",
    "axes[0].scatter(y_test_A, y_pred_A, alpha=0.5, color='#1f77b4', edgecolor='none')\nmax_val = max(max(y_test_A), max(y_pred_A))\naxes[0].plot([0, max_val], [0, max_val], 'r--', linewidth=2, label='Perfect Fit (y=x)')\naxes[0].set_xlabel('Actual Total Diagnoses', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\naxes[0].set_ylabel('Predicted Total Diagnoses', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\naxes[0].set_title(f'Path A: Prediction vs Actual (R² = {r2_A:.4f})', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\naxes[0].legend()\naxes[0].grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n\n# Plot 2: Residual Distribution\naxes[1].hist(residuals_A, bins=40, color='#2ca02c', alpha=0.7, edgecolor='black')\naxes[1].axvline(x=0, color='red', linestyle='--', linewidth=2, label='Zero Error')\naxes[1].set_xlabel('Residual (Actual - Predicted)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\naxes[1].set_ylabel('Frequency', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\naxes[1].set_title('Path A: Distribution of Prediction Errors', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\naxes[1].legend()\naxes[1].grid(True, alpha=0.3, axis='y')\n\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n\nprint(f\"\\n✓ Path A visualization complete\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Part 3: PATH B - Mortality Risk Prediction (XGBoost Classifier)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Problem Statement\n",
    "**Predict**: `is_deceased` (binary: 0=Alive, 1=Deceased)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Critical Challenge**: Extreme class imbalance\n",
    "- 98.1% of patients are Alive (class 0)\n",
    "- 1.9% of patients are Deceased (class 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why Imbalance Matters\n",
    "A naive classifier that **always predicts \"Alive\"** would achieve 98% accuracy without learning anything useful!\n",
    "\n",
    "### Solution Strategy\n",
    "1. **Compute imbalance weight**: Scale the minority class penalty\n",
    "2. **Use PR-AUC metric** instead of accuracy\n",
    "3. **Add clinical features** for better signal\n",
    "4. **Optimize decision threshold** for deployment"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 3.1: Handle Class Imbalance via Scale Weighting"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_calls": [
   {
    "cell_type": "code",
    "execution_count": null,
    "metadata": {},
    "outputs": [],
    "source": [
    "# Split data for Path B\n",
    "X_train_B, X_test_B, y_train_B, y_test_B = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X_engineered, y_path_B, test_size=0.2, random_state=42\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Re-enforce categorical dtypes\n",
    "cat_cols = X_train_B.select_dtypes(include=['object', 'category']).columns.tolist()\n",
    "for col in cat_cols:\n",
    "    X_train_B[col] = X_train_B[col].astype('category')\n",
    "    X_test_B[col] = X_test_B[col].astype('category')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate exact class imbalance ratio\n",
    "num_alive = np.sum(y_train_B == 0)\n",
    "num_deceased = np.sum(y_train_B == 1)\n",
    "imbalance_weight = num_alive / num_deceased\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📊 PATH B CLASS DISTRIBUTION ANALYSIS\")\n",
    "print(f\"═\" * 50)\n",
    "print(f\"Total Training Samples:      {len(y_train_B):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  • Alive (class 0):         {num_alive:,} ({num_alive/len(y_train_B)*100:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"  • Deceased (class 1):      {num_deceased:,} ({num_deceased/len(y_train_B)*100:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\n⚖️  Imbalance Ratio (scale_pos_weight): {imbalance_weight:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   → Missing 1 deceased = as bad as missing {imbalance_weight:.0f} alive patients\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 3.2: Train Baseline Classifier (Demographics Only)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Train baseline model without clinical features\n",
    "print(\"\\n🚀 Training Baseline Classifier (demographics + exposome only)...\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "model_B_baseline = xgb.XGBClassifier(\n",
    "    n_estimators=300,\n",
    "    learning_rate=0.02,\n",
    "    max_depth=5,\n",
    "    subsample=0.8,\n",
    "    colsample_bytree=0.8,\n",
    "    scale_pos_weight=imbalance_weight,  # Critical: penalize missing deceased cases\n",
    "    objective=\"binary:logistic\",\n",
    "    eval_metric=\"logloss\",\n",
    "    enable_categorical=True,\n",
    "    random_state=42,\n",
    "    verbosity=0\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "model_B_baseline.fit(X_train_B, y_train_B)\nprint(\"✓ Model training complete\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Generate predictions\n",
    "y_prob_B = model_B_baseline.predict_proba(X_test_B)[:, 1]  # Get probability of class 1\n",
    "y_pred_B = model_B_baseline.predict(X_test_B)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate metrics\n",
    "roc_auc_B = roc_auc_score(y_test_B, y_prob_B)\n",
    "pr_auc_B = average_precision_score(y_test_B, y_prob_B)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📊 PATH B BASELINE RESULTS:\")\n",
    "print(f\"═\" * 50)\n",
    "print(f\"ROC-AUC Score:           {roc_auc_B:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"PR-AUC (Avg Precision):  {pr_auc_B:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📋 Classification Report:\")\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test_B, y_pred_B, target_names=['Alive', 'Deceased']))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 3.3: Visualize Baseline Performance"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_calls": [
   {
    "cell_type": "code",
    "execution_count": null,
    "metadata": {},
    "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(16, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 1: Confusion Matrix\n",
    "cm_B = confusion_matrix(y_test_B, y_pred_B)\n",
    "sns.heatmap(cm_B, annot=True, fmt='d', cmap='Blues', cbar=False, ax=axes[0],\n",
    "            xticklabels=['Predicted Alive', 'Predicted Deceased'],\n",
    "            yticklabels=['Actual Alive', 'Actual Deceased'],\n",
    "            annot_kws={'size': 12, 'fontweight': 'bold'})\naxes[0].set_title('Confusion Matrix (Threshold = 0.50)', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 2: Precision-Recall Curve\n",
