    "### Step 3.5: Threshold Optimization for Deployment\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Principle**: The default 0.50 threshold is mathematically arbitrary.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Clinical Trade-off**:\n",
    "- **High threshold** (e.g., 0.70) → Fewer false alarms, but miss high-risk patients\n",
    "- **Low threshold** (e.g., 0.20) → Catch more terminal cases, but more false alarms\n",
    "\n",
    "**Medical Reality**: A false alarm (re-checking a healthy patient) costs nothing. Missing a death is catastrophic.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Our Strategy**: Use **Youden's J-Statistic** to find the mathematically optimal point on the ROC curve."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_calls": [
   {
    "cell_type": "code",
    "execution_count": null,
    "metadata": {},
    "outputs": [],
    "source": [
    "from sklearn.metrics import roc_curve\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate ROC curve\n",
    "fpr, tpr, roc_thresholds = roc_curve(y_test_Bc, y_prob_Bc)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Apply Youden's J-Statistic: J = Sensitivity + Specificity - 1\nyoudens_j = tpr - fpr\nbest_idx = np.argmax(youdens_j)\noptimal_threshold_youden = roc_thresholds[best_idx]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sweep alternative thresholds manually\nthresholds_to_test = np.linspace(0.01, 0.99, 100)\nthreshold_results = []\n",
    "\nfor t in thresholds_to_test:\n",
    "    y_pred_custom = (y_prob_Bc >= t).astype(int)\n",
    "    cm = confusion_matrix(y_test_Bc, y_pred_custom)\n",
    "    tn, fp, fn, tp = cm.ravel()\n",
    "    p = precision_score(y_test_Bc, y_pred_custom, zero_division=0)\n",
    "    r = recall_score(y_test_Bc, y_pred_custom, zero_division=0)\n",
    "    threshold_results.append({\n",
    "        'Threshold': t,\n",
    "        'TP': tp, 'FP': fp, 'FN': fn, 'TN': tn,\n",
    "        'Precision': p, 'Recall': r\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\ndf_thresholds = pd.DataFrame(threshold_results)\n",
    "\nprint(f\"\\n🎯 THRESHOLD OPTIMIZATION RESULTS\")\n",
    "print(f\"═\" * 50)\nprint(f\"\\nYouden's J-Statistic Optimal Threshold: {optimal_threshold_youden:.4f}\")\nprint(f\"  → TPR at optimal: {tpr[best_idx]:.4f}\")\nprint(f\"  → FPR at optimal: {fpr[best_idx]:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n# Find recommended threshold for clinical deployment\nrecommended_threshold = 0.20  # Conservative for medical setting\nrecommended_row = df_thresholds[df_thresholds['Threshold'] >= recommended_threshold].iloc[0]\n",
    "\nprint(f\"\\n💊 Recommended Clinical Deployment Threshold: {recommended_threshold:.2f}\")\nprint(f\"  → True Positives (caught deceased):  {int(recommended_row['TP'])} / 71\")\nprint(f\"  → False Positives (false alarms):    {int(recommended_row['FP'])}\")\nprint(f\"  → Recall (Sensitivity):              {recommended_row['Recall']:.2%} (catch rate)\")\nprint(f\"  → Precision:                         {recommended_row['Precision']:.4f}\")"
   ]
